# --- 6. sqlx migration sources: official platform family (ticket 35, D-004) ---
# sqlx::migrate! embeds these .sql bytes and their SHA-384 checksums into the
# binary at compile time. The official openai/codex Windows CLI is built from
# a Windows checkout whose default core.autocrlf=true converts these files to
# CRLF, so its embedded checksum family is CRLF there and LF on Linux/macOS.
# The fork must embed the same family to coexist on one shared home: these
# six directories request plain text normalization with the eol attribute
# left UNSPECIFIED (!eol overrides the section-1 eol=lf), so the checkout
# line endings follow the local git configuration exactly like an official
# build machine. Repository blobs stay LF; only the checkout side is native.
# Do NOT pin eol=lf here: that re-introduces the ticket 25 LF lock that
# stranded shared homes in the wrong family (docs/fork-checksum-family.md).
# CI guards this in both layers: fork-health asserts the per-platform
# checkout bytes; fork-cli-test-release byte-scans the release binaries
# for the embedded SHA-384 digests.
codex-rs/state/migrations/*.sql text !eol
codex-rs/state/logs_migrations/*.sql text !eol
codex-rs/state/goals_migrations/*.sql text !eol
codex-rs/state/memory_migrations/*.sql text !eol
codex-rs/state/queue_migrations/*.sql text !eol
codex-rs/state/thread_history_migrations/*.sql text !eol

# --- 7. Upstream LF pin (kept verbatim from upstream/main, merge 2026-09-12) ---
third_party/voice/sources.json text eol=lf
